# <%= current_page.data.title %>

Use this guide to trial [browser file pickup](../supported-patterns/pull-from-presigned-url.html)
in development. No recipients are enabled by default.

## Configure a recipient

1. Confirm the test user can sign in to
   [the development Transfer web app](https://web.development.file-transfer.service.justice.gov.uk).
   Use a group from `modules/transfer-web-app-identity-configuration`. New application
   assignments belong in the root configuration and must be deployed there first.
2. Agree the clean-file prefix and Slack channel. Add a recipient to
   `modules/authenticated-pickup-configuration/locals-development.tf`:

   ```hcl
   test-pickup = {
     prefix = "<approved-clean-prefix>/"
     groups = ["integration-hub"]
   }
   ```

   Replace the example prefix with an existing shared dispatch entry. The group must
   be approved for that prefix; its existing application assignment is not sufficient.
3. Refresh the branch against main and review a fresh development plan. Check that
   each read grant is limited to the intended recipient directory, then apply the
   `pull-from-presigned-url` component through the platform workflow.
4. In Secrets Manager, set `integration-hub-file-transfer/slack-pickup/test-pickup` to
   `{"url":"<approved Slack incoming webhook URL>"}`. Keep this value out of source
   control and logs. The channel will receive the file's bucket and path.
5. In the matching file-dispatch secret, set `notifications.slack` to `"test-pickup"`.
   Preserve the existing action and other settings. Edit the actual secret: Terraform
   ignores subsequent changes to its initial value.
6. Upload a new non-sensitive file under the approved prefix. Existing events retain
   their original dispatch configuration, so use a new transfer for the test.

## Check the result

- The file is copied before Slack announces it. Follow the portal link, find the
  bucket/path from the message and compare the downloaded file with the original.
- An authorised group member can read that recipient's directory. Another app user
  cannot list or download it, including when given the Slack link.
- Upload and delete fail, and a second recipient's directory remains inaccessible.
- Test a small file and a file larger than 5 GiB. Both downloads must match their sources.
- Keep a test download URL private. A new request after five minutes should fail;
  returning to the portal should allow a fresh download. Check for cached-link problems.
- Test removal of group access and record how long already-issued credentials work.
- Quarantined files produce no pickup notification. Confirm the seven-day lifecycle
  behaviour meets the customer's needs; it does not enforce an exact access cutoff.

These checks are required before customer access. Unit tests cannot establish live
Identity Center permissions or the Transfer web app's behaviour.

## If a notification is missing

Check the notifier's logs, processing queue and dead-letter queues. The function
validates the source prefix and immutable object and dispatch-secret versions. Failed
copies do not notify. Events older than 12 hours are skipped because clean files have
short retention, so investigate delays promptly.

Receipts prevent routine duplicate notifications for 14 days. A retry reuses an
existing copy rather than extending its collection window. An uncertain Slack response
can still result in a duplicate message. Large files use multipart copy; interrupted
uploads have a one-day cleanup rule.

Dead-letter queue alarms go to the existing PagerDuty topics: low priority outside
production, high priority in production. Other function and queue alarms notify low
priority in production. Use the
[queue investigation guide](investigating-and-replaying-file-transfer-dlq-messages.html)
when a message needs replaying.

## Moving from the earlier development page

The new design removes the custom HTTP API, sign-in page and download Lambda.
The old execute-api link is retired; `portal_url` points to the Transfer web app.
Review those removals in the plan. The pickup bucket should remain, along with the
root Transfer and Identity Center resources. Do not apply an old saved plan.
Existing copies outside recipient directories are not covered by the new grants.

## Run the unit tests

From the `modernisation-platform-environments` checkout:

```sh
PYTHONPATH=terraform/environments/integration-hub-file-transfer/pull-from-presigned-url/lambda/notifier \
  python3 -m unittest discover -s terraform/environments/integration-hub-file-transfer/pull-from-presigned-url/lambda/notifier/tests -v
```

A [shared Python testing approach](python-unit-test-automation.html) is proposed for
all file-transfer functions. It replaces the pickup-specific workflow proposal; the
automation and Slack failure alerts described there are not deployed by this PR.
